On Dec 20, 2007 1:28 AM, komfo,amonan <komfoamonan@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> I think "live" is built into {tigni}.

I'm not sure. The definition says "for/before audience x3". If it were
just "before", it would have to be live, but "for" seems to admit
pre-recorded performances too.

> Thus:
>
> mi pu te tigni fi la cakla respa .i je ba za bo mi ve skina le se go'i
> I saw Chocolate Reptile live, then later saw the film of the performance.

I think that would work with that context. Perhaps {narpruvei},
"not pre-recorded" can be used if there is a need to be more
explicit.

